    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson** serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Gunnar Henderson** (74.86) is a high-conviction start; despite facing a capable arm in Freddy Peralta, the +14% dynamic platoon edge and the opportunity to exploit a slow delivery\u2014which elevates his stolen base potential\u2014make him our top-scoring asset. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) draws the most favorable matchup of the day against Bradford. His score is bolstered by a significant +19% SP skill advantage and a park factor favorable to his profile, positioning him as the centerpiece of our infield production. **Jackson Merrill** (69.72) rounds out our elite tier, as his +13% dynamic platoon edge against Bibee compensates for a modest base projection, making him a high-upside play in the outfield.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Coby Mayo** (42.34) serving as the most notable exclusion. While **Coby Mayo** maintained an acceptable profile, he ultimately fell short of our rotational threshold due to a negative platoon split against Peralta and a suboptimal spot in the bottom of the order, which suppressed his run-scoring probability. We continue to manage our volume carefully, keeping **Wade Meckler** sidelined as his sub-40 efficiency score fails to meet our daily requirement. Meanwhile, we remain in a holding pattern regarding the health of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez**, both of whom are currently unavailable and remain inactive on our bench.\n\nManagers should monitor the risk profile surrounding **Andy Pages** (46.78) and **Kyle Tucker** (51.57), both of whom face Henderson today. While their raw projections remain serviceable, the +19% skill penalty associated with this matchup necessitates cautious expectations for their performance. Conversely, we are banking on the high-floor versatility of **Drake Baldwin** (54.13) to anchor the catcher position; his placement in the leadoff spot provides a +10% order bonus that should mitigate the difficulty of his matchup against Soroka. We are effectively avoiding high-risk starts in favor of maximizing efficiency, ensuring that every slot occupied is optimized to preserve our games-played cap while chasing marginal gains in the SB category.",
